## UI Craft: Khmer sign-up card

Stack: vanilla HTML/CSS · Theme: light + dark · States: complete

**Assumptions:** you said this is a prototype, so I used the skill's default tokens (no `design/` foundation, no palette question). The Khmer copy is placeholder text that you should replace.

## Tokens & architecture
- Tokens use the `design-system` names: `--color-surface-*`, `--color-text-*`, `--color-border-*`, `--color-action-primary-*`, `--r-*`, `--z-*`.
- Dark mode follows `prefers-color-scheme`. `data-theme="light"` or `"dark"` on `<html>` overrides it.
- Khmer text uses one `line-height: 1.6` and `letter-spacing: 0` under `:lang(km)`. Heading tracking is Latin-only.
- The font stack uses installed fonts only, with no external fonts or libraries.
- The card is fluid (`min(420px, 100%)`), so it has no horizontal scroll from 390px to 1440px.
- The button and input are at least 44px tall, with a 2px `:focus-visible` outline.
- Motion is `transform` and `opacity` only, and it is turned off under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

