## States & keyboard
- **Keyboard:** Tab moves through the field and the button, and Enter submits. The email field takes focus again after an invalid submit.
- **Default, hover, active, disabled:** all are styled. Disabled styling is in the CSS, but the prototype never sets it.
- **Focus:** the 2px `:focus-visible` outline is used on both controls.
- **Error:** an empty or invalid email shows an inline Khmer message in a `role="status"` region. The typed text is kept and the field gets `aria-invalid`.
- **Success:** a confirmation message replaces the error.
- **Not included:** this is a single-field form with no data loading, so there is no skeleton, empty or retry state. Add those when you connect a real endpoint.

## Verification & open questions
- **Not run in a browser.** I did not render it at 1440px or 390px, and I did not check the console.
- **Contrast pairs:** from the default token values, muted text on the surface is about 7:1 in light mode and about 7.5:1 in dark mode. The primary button is near-black on white or white on near-black. The 3:1 border/focus pairs are also from token values.
- **Khmer font:** the card uses whichever Khmer font is installed (Noto Sans Khmer, Khmer OS and so on). If you want a guaranteed look, you'd need to add a font, which I did not do without your say-so.
- **Placeholder copy:** replace the Khmer title and paragraph with your product's wording. I used no invented metrics or testimonials.
- **Tokens:** this prototype defines its own tokens. When a `design/tokens.css` exists, delete the `:root` blocks and link that file.
